DESCRIPTION:If you haven’t heard of Lace Larrabee\, you will soon. Lace i
 s a nationally touring comedian\, actress\, and host whose debut comedy alb
 um\, White Trash Cinderella\, produced by 800 Pound Gorilla Records\, seale
 d the number one spot on the comedy charts. The  accompanying YouTube spec
 ial  amassed over 1.9 million views and counting.\n\nA former southern bea
 uty queen\, Lace ditched the pageants but kept her dominant stage presence\
 , unrivaled timing and trademark sass. As a season 17 semifinalist on Ameri
 ca’s Got Talent\, America loved her charming wit so much\, NBC brought he
 r back to roast Simon Cowell alongside Roastmaster General himself\, Jeff R
 oss. Lace turned her appearance on AGT into a Vegas residency as host of Am
 erica’s Got Talent Superstars Live.\n\nFor over 13 years\, Lace has been 
 honing her self-deprecating humor and hilarious personal anecdotes into a s
 tyle that is fiercely her own. Lace can captivate a room and garner laughs 
 as big as her personality.  From tales of growing up in a trailer to relat
 able observations on friends\, family\, love and aging\, Lace turns life’
 s humiliating moments into an indomitable act of comedy. Lace’s candor\, 
 perspicacity\, and refreshingly real takes on life make comedians want to b
 e her\, audiences want to be best friends with her.\n\nLace is a regular fa
 vorite on Sirius XM. Lace’s charisma radiates and her writing and deliver
 y are undeniable. Lace has found her voice and is passionate about empoweri
 ng others to find and use theirs too through founding Atlanta's #1 comedy c
 lass\,  Laugh Lab .\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event
 /lace-larrabee-returns-to-bloomington/
